ncroaching forces of the Ostrogothic King Ermanaric culminated in a pivotal conflict that profoundly shaped the geopolitical landscape of the Pontic Steppe and the Roman frontier, marking a critical moment in the period often referred to as the Völkerwanderung, or Migration Age.

Around 370 CE, Boz led the Antes in a desperate struggle against the formidable Ostrogothic expansion. Following a period of intense resistance or an initial but ultimately unsuccessful military campaign, the Antes suffered a decisive defeat. The Gothic king Ermanaric, seeking to consolidate his power and intimidate other tribal groups, captured Boz and, according to the historical accounts of Jordanes in his work *Getica* (Chapter 24), had him, along with his sons and seventy nobles, crucified. This brutal act was intended to break the spirit of the Antes and assert Gothic dominance over the vast region north of the Black Sea.

Boz's martyrdom, whether a precise historical fact or an embellished legend, became a potent symbol of proto-Slavic resistance against Germanic hegemony. His defeat and execution contributed to the temporary subjugation of the Antes under Gothic rule, which in turn accelerated the westward movement of various Germanic tribes, including the Goths themselves, eventually putting immense pressure on the borders of the Roman Empire. The subsequent arrival of the Huns shortly after 370 CE would dramatically alter this delicate balance of power, but Boz's stand against Ermanaric foreshadowed the complex inter-ethnic struggles that characterized the late Classical period and the dawn of the Early Middle Ages."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-28T01:21:08Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#28307147417", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "319 CE"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "319 CE"}], "newValue": ["The expanding power and territorial ambitions of the Ostrogothic Kingdom under Ermanaric directly threatened the independence of the Antes.", "The established geopolitical presence of the Antes as a significant tribal confederation positioned them as a natural barrier to Gothic expansion eastward.", "The broader period of the Migration Age (Völkerwanderung) created a volatile environment of shifting alliances and frequent conflicts among various barbarian groups."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-28T01:21:08Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#28307147417", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "370 CE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "370 CE"}], "newValue": ["Boz's 